include "markers.mereo"

-- `leave pick` from inside a COLD road -- a road is a scope, so this is the
-- road's own break: release what THIS ROAD took and rejoin the merge, without
-- running the rest of the arm. The pass's `o` and the program's `keep` stay
-- live, so the loop keeps going.
--
-- The road runs on the middle pass only, and `late` is opened after the leave,
-- so it must never be reached: 101 closes on the two hot passes and never in
-- the road.
-- Expect 101 103, then 105 102 103, then 101 103, then 104.
--
-- Two shapes here are deliberate, both learned from mereocheck rejecting the
-- first draft. The road holds TWO markers: with one it did exactly the work of
-- the likely road and ended at the same label, so GCC if-converted the pair
-- into a cmov of the descriptor. And the guard reads the loop counter, not
-- argc: a loop-invariant guard let GCC UNSWITCH the loop into two specialised
-- copies, which dissolves the road just as thoroughly. The trip count comes
-- from argc so the loop cannot be unrolled and the guard folded.
program (arguments) is
  keep is adopted mark_d (descriptor is 104)
  n is arguments.count
  i is 0

  serve goes
    o is adopted mark_c (descriptor is 103)
    pick likely goes
      h is adopted mark_a (descriptor is 101)
    end
    i is i + 1
    repeat serve when i < n + 2
  end

  pick when i == 1 goes
    c is adopted mark_b (descriptor is 102)
    e is adopted mark_e (descriptor is 105)
    leave pick when n < 9
    late is adopted mark_a (descriptor is 101)
  end
end
